# Hosts Worker VMs may reach through the gateway's forward proxy.
# One rule per line: a host name, or *. and a domain for its subdomains,
# optionally followed by :port. Without a port a rule permits 443 and 80.
# Never list github.com, or the hosts of an LLM provider whose credential the
# gateway holds: a CONNECT tunnel cannot remove a caller token or any other
# credential, and the gateway serves them at git.<domain> and llm.<domain>.

# Harness logins on the Worker. Without a gateway credential for their
# provider, Claude Code and Codex use the operator's logins on the Worker's
# machine and reach their providers through this proxy. Remove a harness's
# hosts when the gateway holds that provider's credential, a subscription
# login or an API key (llm_providers in usine.yaml).

# Claude Code with a Claude subscription: the API, and the OAuth token
# endpoint that claude auth login and token refreshes call.
api.anthropic.com
platform.claude.com

# Codex with a ChatGPT plan: the ChatGPT API, and the device-code login and
# token refreshes.
chatgpt.com
auth.openai.com

